.el .ds Aq '
.TH photocraft-cli-batch 1  "batch " 
.SH NAME
photocraft\-cli\-batch \- Apply an action list to every image in a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBphotocraft\-cli batch\fR [\fB\-\-action\fR] [\fB\-\-in\-place\fR] [\fB\-\-recursive\fR] [\fB\-\-naming\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-serial\fR] [\fB\-\-stop\-on\-error\fR] [\fB\-\-error\-log\fR] [\fB\-\-approve\-high\-memory\fR] [\fB\-\-gpu\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-gpu\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-quality\fR] [\fB\-\-tiff\-layers\fR] [\fB\-\-tiff\-compression\fR] [\fB\-\-tiff\-transparency\fR] [\fB\-\-tiff\-pyramid\fR] [\fB\-\-tga\-bits\fR] [\fB\-\-dpx\-bits\fR] [\fB\-\-dds\-compression\fR] [\fB\-\-dds\-mipmaps\fR] [\fB\-\-jpeg\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-pcraft\-full\-composite\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-actions\fR> <\fB\-\-in\fR> <\fB\-\-out\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Apply an action list to every image in a directory
.PP
A Photoshop Actions file (.atn) is a set: its action \-\-action names plays, as below. JSON steps are [id, params] pairs, {"command": id, "params": {…}} objects or bare ids, as a recorded action or droplet stores them (a list, or wrapped in {"actions": …}, {"steps": …} or a droplet). An Actions set (the Actions panel\*(Aqs actions.json, {"actions": [{"name", "steps"}…]}) plays the action \-\-action names (needed when the set holds more than one) with the whole set loaded, so its steps can play other actions of the set.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-actions\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
The action list: actions.json, a droplet, or a Photoshop Actions file (.atn)
.TP
\fB\-\-action\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which action of an Actions set to play
.TP
\fB\-\-in\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The folder of images to process
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The folder to write the results to, as <stem>.<ext>
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
An \-\-out folder that is the \-\-in folder is refused, as the results would replace the originals; \-\-in\-place allows it
.TP
\fB\-\-recursive\fR
Include images in subfolders; every result goes straight into \-\-out, so a later file of the same name replaces an earlier one
.TP
\fB\-\-naming\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR
Name each result with Batch tokens such as {name}, {serial}, {date}, and {ext}
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-serial\fR \fI<1\-4294967295>\fR
First serial number used by \-\-naming
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\-on\-error\fR
Stop after the first failed input
.TP
\fB\-\-error\-log\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write failed inputs and reasons to this text file
.TP
\fB\-\-approve\-high\-memory\fR
Explicitly approve high\-memory PSD/PSB imports within the hard memory budget
.TP
\fB\-\-gpu\fR
Prefer GPU rendering, falling back to CPU when unavailable or unsupported
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-gpu\fR
Use CPU rendering, overriding PHOTOCRAFT_GPU
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<EXT>\fR
Output format, overriding the output\*(Aqs extension (png, jpg, tif, webp, …)
.TP
\fB\-\-quality\fR \fI<1\-100>\fR
JPEG or WebP quality, 1\-100. A WebP written with a quality is lossy, without one lossless
.TP
\fB\-\-tiff\-layers\fR
Keep the layers in TIFF output (Photoshop layer data); TIFF output is flat without it
.TP
\fB\-\-tiff\-compression\fR \fI<none|lzw|zip>\fR
Compress TIFF output: none (the default), lzw or zip
.TP
\fB\-\-tiff\-transparency\fR \fI<on|off>\fR
TIFF Save Transparency: on keeps the transparency (ahead of any alpha or spot channels), off composites the image over white. Without it: kept unless the document has alpha or spot channels
.TP
\fB\-\-tiff\-pyramid\fR
Also write a TIFF image pyramid: half\-size copies after the full image
.TP
\fB\-\-tga\-bits\fR \fI<24|32>\fR
A TGA\*(Aqs bits per pixel: 32 writes the alpha channel (or else the transparency) as its alpha, 24 none. Without it: 32 with an alpha channel or transparency, else 24
.TP
\fB\-\-dpx\-bits\fR \fI<8|10|12|16>\fR
A DPX\*(Aqs bits per sample. Without it: 8 for an 8\-bit document, else 16
.TP
\fB\-\-dds\-compression\fR \fI<none|bc1|bc2|bc3>\fR
A DDS texture\*(Aqs compression: none (uncompressed, the default), bc1 (DXT1: alpha on or off), bc2 (DXT3) or bc3 (DXT5)
.TP
\fB\-\-dds\-mipmaps\fR
Also write a DDS texture\*(Aqs full mip chain
.TP
\fB\-\-jpeg\-format\fR \fI<baseline|optimized|progressive>\fR
A JPEG\*(Aqs scans, as JPEG Options picks them: baseline (the default), optimized (Huffman tables fitted to the image; RGB is written 4:2:0 and keeps the standard tables, so only Gray and CMYK shrink) or progressive
.TP
\fB\-\-pcraft\-full\-composite\fR
Request the flattened document at its canvas size in .pcraft output as composite/full.png; it may be omitted. Check the manifest\*(Aqs full_composite member
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
